CSS opacity applies to an element and its contents as a group: the element establishes a stacking context,
paints itself and its descendants into a layer at full alpha, and composites that layer at its opacity. RmlUi
inherited opacity into each element's vertex alpha, so a descendant declaring its own (a progress bar inside a
fading overlay) replaced its ancestors' and overlapping translucent boxes showed through each other. Opacity is
no longer inherited; a fully transparent group paints nothing.
CSS Color 4: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-4/#transparency

